    "title": "Palm Springs reggaeton scene mirrors Karol G amid Coachella moment",
    "text": "COACHELLAKarol G will make history at Coachella. What that means for reggaeton Brian BlueskyePalm Springs Desert SunApril 9, 2026, 10:27 a.m. PTKarol G’s upcoming headlining performances during Coachella 2026 aren’t just milestones for her as the first Latina headliner. They also reflect the continuing rise of reggaeton on the world stage, which is mirrored in the nightlife culture of the Coachella Valley.Her presence at the festival also marks a shift in a genre that has been dominated by men. Reggaeton’s earliest stars, such as Daddy Yankee and Don Omar, shaped the sound’s identity. Karol G is a sign of a new era where woman aren't just participating in the genre, they're right at the center of it.Already a subscriber? Sign inTwo ways to continue readingPay Annually$119SAVE 50% versus MonthlySubscribeSubscribers getBEST DEALFull access to desertsun.com including articles, videos, and moreA subscription to shareAccess to the eNewspaperShow featuresMonthly$1for the first monthSubscribeSubscribers getFull access to desertsun.com including articles, videos, and moreA subscription to shareAccess to the eNewspaperShow featuresInterested in other subscriptions? Learn more",
